{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559377-instinct-paths-and-functioning","id":1559377,"title":"Instinct Paths and functioning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-12T12:32:14-07:00","id":1559377,"title":"Instinct Paths and functioning","content":"How do Paths and Roads that follow Instinct function? It seems that the slightest insult will set you off, which means attacking everyone, even your pack (frenzied don't care about vinculum ratings or blood bonds if I recall correctly).<br /> <br /> I don't imagine Sabbat being super polite to each other but it seems like they would have to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28717-tywyll","name":"Tywyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T13:21:05-07:00","id":1559379,"title":"","content":"Okay so Forum ate it... happens. Remember folks, never edit your posts...<br /> <br /> Lets try this again, shall we? Good.<br /> <br /> So, Instinct is controling the Beast by familiarity rather than denial<br /> <br /> My advice is not play it as &quot;edgy human who is angry all the time.&quot; It's deeper - Instinct doesn't mean you're stupid or uncontrolled; it means you're <i>better</i> at working <i>with</i> the Beast. Remember, Paths could be quite philosophical, the Path of Caine or Metamorphosis, not just survivalist/animalistic like the Path of the Beast for example<br /> It mostly maifest in body language - moving with predatory grace or coiled tension. Staring too intently. Reacting to different stimuli (blood, danger, dominance) immediately and often physically. You might sniff the air, bare fangs subtly, or shift posture like an animal sensing territory and presence.<br /> You have the <b>presence</b> of a Predator<br /> <br /> High-Instinct vampire (4\u20135) is actually quite good at staying composed against everyday annoyances while still being able to unleash controlled predatory fury when it serves them<br /> Minor provocations like a rude comment, a bumped shoulder, spilled drink or similar things are often difficulty 3\u20134 and followers have Instinct high enough to ignore these entirely if they choose. But may growl or bare their fangs, the eyes flashes like an anoyed big feline or wolf but not really bothers to actualyl attacks the source of the anoyance<br /> Real insults like public humiliation, betrayal by a packmate, serious threat are usually difficulty 6\u20138. These will trigger frenzy, that is true... but the here comes the &quot;benefit&quot; of Instinct in the picture.<br /> Instinct allows the character to harness the Beast's destructive power - you can &quot;ride the wave&quot;, it lets you direct it.<br /> You can focus all your fury on the one who insulted you, while leaving allies untouched or intimidate everyone with your bared power insted turning the haven into a Tarantino's wet dream, feet included. The Beast is a complicated entity and depending of what angle you aproach it (or source) it could range from bestial force of nature (in that case dominating and displaying its superioirty by force or other ways satsify its urges) to the Wraith's Shadow/Kuei-jin's P'o like basically sentinent dark part of yourself you even able to communicate in some cases - there are Flaws/merits and backgrounds to flesh out your Beast if you go to that<br /> And of course the Path in question effects the situation in a degree someone on the Metamorphois wil lreact differently than one on the Caine or the Grey Hunter or Pleasure<br /> <br /> In any case usuall an insult doesn\u2019t make a Vampire on the Path using Instinct to \u201close it like a human and having a tantrum.\u201d It makes the Beast rise, yes, and the vampire decides whether to let it surge in a useful direction or suppress the minor ones.<br /> You are inense, with a dominating, frightening predatory presence, you might growl a warning instead of politely asking someone to stop, or might smile with too many teeth when provoked - imagine an anyoed cat or dog, as I said before. The Beast regardless of its type is Proud and minor things simply not worth its time. Your time.<br /> With High Instinct and strong Path adherence your character usually seems dangerously calm most of the time, but when the Beast is unleashed, it is precise, terrifying, and purposeful \u2014 like a wolf that chooses exactly which throat to tear out.<br /> <br /> The point is, you feel and act inhuman in a very specific way - you are more direct, passionate, and primal in even small things, in daily behavioral things (again depends on the Road a bit). You don\u2019t suppress anger or hunger, you knowledge it openly. But this lack of denial gives you a form of control. An unspoken agreement if you will between your Beast and you, your dark shadow and higher intelect; the two blend, the Predator with an Intelect<br /> Actually the Yautja are a very good example of someone using Instinct if you ask me<br /> \u200b<br /> But of course every traveller of a Road have a first step<br /> <br /> If your character has low Instinct (1\u20132), then yes \u2014 even moderate insults will trigger frenzy and riding the wave will be unreliable and more often than not you fail to do it, making you feel more out of control and \u201cbeast-heavy.\u201d As Instinct rises through experience and roleplay, you become better at directing the monster you\u2019ve embraced<br /> But it is part of the fun (if you not skip it and have a high Instinct character at creation) to learn the Path and accepting your Instincts - this of course have the high chance you fail on your path or ends up with a vampire lost to the Beast - or some friends torn pieces - but it is part of the Story<br /> <br /> This phase, having 1-2 Instinct is a very specific, uncomfortable \u201cin-between\u201d state. Your character has chosen to walk away from Humanity and Self-Control, but they have not yet fully surrendered to the Beast. Mechanically and narratively, this makes them feel raw, clumsy, and constantly at war with themselves \u2014 even though the Path philosophy says they shouldn\u2019t be fighting at all.<br /> This means the slightest insult really does set you off \u2014 exactly as you feared in your earlier question. A mortal bartender calling you \u201cweirdo\u201d or a packmate making a casual joke at your expense can send you straight into rage frenzy with almost no warning.<br /> Raising Instinct is not automatic. It requires deliberate roleplay, Path adherence, and Storyteller approval if you asks me; the character must actively practice letting the Beast &quot;speak&quot; instead of fighting it. You have to deliberately expose yourself to small triggers (hunger, minor insults) and try to feel the surge without immediately suppressing it.<br /> You even might have to seek out a mentor (older Path follower, Pack Priest, or even a wild animal they observe for hours) to learn how to \u201clisten\u201d rather than command the Beast.<br /> When the Beast rises you close your eyes and whisper \u201cGuide me\u2026\u201d instead of clamping down. On a successful ride you manage to walk across the room and feed neatly on the prepared vessel instead of mauling them, like a predator zoning in on a pciked up prey insted mauling the whole herd. Controlled, deliberate, lethal and efficient. \u200b<br /> <br /> The moments of growth thus should feel almost spiritual: the first time you successfully ride a wave and feel the pure, clean power instead of panic or the night you realize an insult no longer have any meaning it is just an anoyence you can scoff of with a growl or snarl<br /> In time you will become more comfortable with your predatory nature; no more apologizing after outbursts, no more trying to \u201cfix\u201d their behavior like a human, the Instinct trait should/could become stronger, higher and with it your mastery and control that came with the familiarity and acceptance; you starts feeling <i>good</i> in frenzy. Control becomes reliable. You begin to look down on low-Instinct neonates the way a seasoned Sabbat looks at a Camarilla fledgling<br /> Low Instinct is the \u201cpainful birth\u201d phase of becoming a true Predator (or Monster, dealers chocie);\u200b It\u2019s frustrating, embarrassing, and full of failure (Starting at Instinct 1 means probably the next 4\u20136 sessions feel like a disaster. Constant accidental violence, packmates getting hurt, Masquerade breaches with the high chence of total falirue and the possibility to lose your character) \u2014 but those failures are exactly what make the later high-Instinct roleplay feel earned and powerful.\u200b in my humble opinion\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T15:00:31-07:00","id":1559380,"title":"","content":"Awesome response, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28717-tywyll","name":"Tywyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T05:02:06-07:00","id":1559412,"title":"","content":"Perhaps only tangentially relevant, but one of the ways I have people roleplay developing alternate virtues is, I'll have their mentor take them to a fire and instead of resisting the beast's fear, they focus on getting to the other side of the fire as an enemy who must be destroyed or prey that must be caught. The idea is to become an intelligent beast rather than a disciplined human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T00:09:34-07:00","id":1561590,"title":"","content":"I'd add: have friends that can beat you.<br /> <br /> The most important thing about following such Paths is to understand that this is exactly the point: you'll frenzy, that's your life now, and you adapt to it.<br /> <br /> A few important points:<ul><li>&quot;Insult&quot; is a personal evaluation. You're not required to see anything in particular as one. What you don't care about causes no roll.</li> <li>Even more important than guiding your Frenzy, the Path helps define what may anger you and what not. Learn what makes you Frenzy.</li> <li>Avoid situations where you can't Frenzy, simple as that. Vampires successful at those paths let other people do what they won't.</li> <li>You can avoid frenzies by avoiding triggers at all. Not easy at first, but you get the hang of it. Watch your environment, see the trigger, avoid.</li> <li>Have people around you that will help. Paths don't require you think everyone should let you be stupid. Recognize social support you need</li> </ul><br /> Sabbat aren't required to be assholes with each other, by the way. You'll probably avoid packs with toxic environments. You know you have a temper and you surround yourself with people who'll help you make it a strength, not idiots begging to get killed.<br /> <br /> Brought to you by someone with anger issues IRL who has to manage frenzies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}